        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Ritter, Penny Marshall, Cassie Yates, Bert Convy, Constance McCashin, Tex Ritter, Jason Ritter, Tyler Ritter\n- Works: Love Thy Neighbor, Three's Company\n- Topics: American television and film acting awards\n\nFacts:\n- John Ritter was born on September 17, 1948, and died on September 11, 2003.\n- John Ritter was an American actor and comedian.\n- John Ritter was the son of singer and actor Tex Ritter.\n- John Ritter was the father of actors Jason Ritter and Tyler Ritter.\n- From 1977 to 1984, John Ritter was best known for playing Jack Tripper on the ABC sitcom Three's Company.\n- In 1984, John Ritter received a Primetime Emmy Award and a Golden Globe Award for Three's Company.\n- Love Thy Neighbor is a 1984 American made-for-television romantic comedy film.\n- Love Thy Neighbor starred John Ritter, Penny Marshall, Cassie Yates, Bert Convy, and Constance McCashin.",
